# Declension: en.wiktionary.org.  A counted noun surfaces in more than one
# form here.  After "pirms"/"pēc" it is the genitive singular when the numeral
# ends in 1 (and is not 11) and the dative plural otherwise ("pirms sekundes",
# "pirms 11 sekundēm").  A bare count admits two registers -- formal genitive
# plural after 11-19 and the round tens, colloquial nominative -- and both ship,
# because nothing in the input says which register the writer used.
# Unicode CLDR 47, locale lv, cldr-units-full/main/lv/units.json,
# duration-second: one "sekunde", other "sekundes", zero "sekunžu".
sekunde
sekundes
sekunžu
sekundēm
sekundi
sekundē
